 the roots is \\( c \\)\n\n    Applying Vieta\u2019s formulas to our equations, we have:\n    \\[\n    p + (-(p + a)) = -a, \\quad p(-a - p) = -15\n    \\]\n\n3. **Setting the equations:**\n\n    To simplify, let\u2019s solve for the roots and coefficients:\n    \\[\n    p(p + a) = 15 \\rightarrow \\text{(1)}\n    \\]\n    \\[\n    q(q + b) = 6 \\rightarrow \\text{(2)}\n    \\]\n    \\[\n    r(r + c) = 27 \\rightarrow \\text{(3)}\n    \\]\n\n4. **Finding possible values of \\( p, q, r \\):**\n\n    - The terms \\( p, q, r \\) are prime numbers since the larger root must be prime:\n    - Considering possible pairs that yield the factorizations of \\( 15, 6, 27 \\):\n\n      From equation (1):\n      \\[\n      p(p + a) = 15 \\implies p \\in \\{3, 5\\} \\text{ giving } a \\in \\{2, 0\\}\n      \\]\n\n      From equation (2):\n      \\[\n      q(q + b) = 6 \\implies q \\in \\{2, 3\\} \\text{ giving } b \\in \\{1, 0\\}\n      \\]\n\n      From equation (3):\n      \\[\n      r(r + c) = 27 \\implies r \\in \\{3, 9\\} \\text{ giving } c \\in \\{6, 0\\}\n      \\]\n\n5. **Determining valid prime roots:**\n\n    We select the roots to satisfy the one known prime (larger root) condition for each:\n    \\(\\boxed{p = 3}, \\quad \\boxed{q = 2}, \\quad \\boxed{r = 3}\\)\n\n6. **Calculating the roots:**\n\n    \\[\n    \\text{For } p = 3 :\n    \\begin{cases}\n    3 + a = 5 & \\Rightarrow a = 2 \\\\\n    \\text{Other root} = -(p + a) = -5\n    \\end{cases}\n    \\]\n\n    \\[\n    \\text{For } q = 2 :\n    \\begin{cases}\n    2 + b = 3 & \\Rightarrow b = 1 \\\\\n    \\text{Other root} = -(q + b) = -3\n    \\end{cases}\n    \\]\n\n    \\[\n    \\text{For } r = 3 :\n    \\begin{cases}\n    3 + c = 9 & \\Rightarrow c = 6 \\\\\n    \\text{Other root} = -(r + c) = -9\n    \\end{cases}\n    \\]\n\n7. **Summing all roots:**\n\n    \\[\n    \\text{Total sum} = 3 + (-5) + 2 + (-3) + 3 + (-9) = -9\n    \\]\n\nConclusion:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-9}\n\\]", "domain": "math", "source": "numina_math", 